10100010  comma_token                  ,
10100011  semicolon_token              ;
10100100  colon_token                  :
10100101  namespace_token              :: -- namespace::object
10100110  method_token                 .  the dot that calls a method on something
10100111  decimal_point_token          .  the dot inside a number, 3.14
10101000  path_separator_token         /  the slash inside a path
10101001  escape_token                 \  the escape inside text
10101010  linux_home_token             ~  the home directory, $HOME
10101011  double_quote_token           "  a string literal starts or ends
10101100  single_quote_token           '
10101101  comment_token                // to the end of the line
10101110  comment_start_token          /*
10101111  comment_end_token            */
10110000  line_end_token               the end of a statement
10110001  end_of_file_token            always the last token
10110010  word_number_token            a satellite word follows as its numbers: #1.5.1
10110011  name_token                   a name the user owns follows, as characters
10110100  number_token                 a number literal follows, as characters
10110101  string_token                 a string literal follows, as characters
10110110  bits_token                   a bits literal follows: x00FF or b1010
10110111  question_token               ?
10111000  arrow_token                  ->
